From 0062de26ea3cc4e1fb4e6ce04d153c1042e7022c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 21:54:01 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Advisor export v2: Live-tab attribution, net liquidation
 value, open entries

- Entries the structure rules don't fit (e.g. Nov 11's 13:30 / 13:35 ICs, puts 55 / calls 50)
  fall back to the Live tab's backtest profiles (profileMatch: leg signature, nearest usual entry
  time, usual credit range), with a confidence and matchSource "live_profile".
- account: Schwab net liquidation value now and at each stored end of day, so the advisor can
  measure drawdown from the NLV high instead of 15 days of book P/L.
- book.open: entries still open with legs, size and open P/L.
All new fields are optional in the contract; read-only, no account identifiers.
